# Skill: feedback-router (PATTERN §19.4, v2.12)

> Adapter Cursor della skill `feedback-router` definita in `.claude/skills/feedback-router.md`.
> Costrutto: Cursor rule `.mdc`. File equivalente Claude Code: `.claude/skills/feedback-router.md`.

Skill di handoff Reviewer → dev-agent. Invocata dall'ultima fase di `code-review-protocol`.

## Input

```python
{"report": <report json>, "tsk": <frontmatter TSK>, "config": <code_quality.router>}
```

## Decisione per verdict

### `verdict: pass` → `action: close`

- Aggiorna frontmatter TSK: `review_status: passed`, `review_iter: <N>`, `review_report: <path>`.
- Append `wiki/log.md` con verdict `pass`.
- Suggerisci in chat: `/promote <wiki-page> approved` se wiki in `review`; chiusura sprint se ultimo TSK.

### `verdict: conditional` → `action: dispatch_dev`

- Determina `target_agent` da `tsk.layer` (be→be-dev, fe→fe-dev, db→db-dev, qa→qa-dev).
- Costruisce `task_package`:
```json
{
  "tsk_id": "<tsk.id>",
  "iter": N,
  "constraint": {"scope": "fix only the findings below; no opportunistic refactor", "max_diff_lines": <config>},
  "actions": [{"rule_id", "rule_ref", "file", "lines", "current_snippet", "expected_fix", "acceptance_criteria"}],
  "report_ref": "code_quality/reports/<tsk_id>-iter-<N>.md",
  "previous_files_modified": [...]
}
```

- **Strategie di batching** (`config.router.strategy`):
  - `all-in-one`: un solo task_package se `len(findings) ≤ batching_split (7)`.
  - `severity-tiered`: split in 3 sub-package (high+critical → medium → low); consegna solo il primo tier.
  - `split-by-area`: N task_package paralleli per modulo (code_path disgiunto).

- Gate umano:
```
REVIEW CONDITIONAL — TSK-XXX iter N
Verdict: conditional (M finding)
Strategy: <strategy>
Target: <target_agent>
Prossima review: iter N+1 / max_iterations
Procedo con dispatch? [y/N]
```

- Aggiorna frontmatter: `review_status: conditional`, `review_iter: N`.
- Append `wiki/log.md` verdict `conditional`.

### `verdict: reject` → `action: escalate_human` (PATTERN §7 r.16)

- Aggiorna frontmatter: `review_status: rejected`, `review_iter: N`.
- Append `wiki/log.md` + marker (`loop_exhausted | no_progress | regression`).
- Mai invocare dev-agent. Mai auto-revert.
- Blocco escalation in chat con next step: re-develop manuale, accept-as-is, rollback.

## QA Failure Routing (EP-029, opt-in `qa_layer.failure_taxonomy.enabled: true`)

Per TSK `layer: qa`, `status: failed`, `failure_classification:` valorizzato:

| `failure_classification` | Destinatario |
|---|---|
| `APPLICATION_BUG` + `tag: be` | `be-dev` |
| `APPLICATION_BUG` + `tag: fe` | `fe-dev` |
| `APPLICATION_BUG` ambiguo | human gate |
| `SSR_BUG` | `fe-dev` + context `"ssr"` |
| `TEST_BUG` | `qa-dev` |
| `INFRASTRUCTURE` | human gate |
| `FLAKY` | quarantena EP-027 (se abilitato) o human gate |

Idempotenza: se `assigned_to:` già valorizzato → skip dispatch.
Audit: record JSONL in `analytics/events/qa-events.jsonl`.

## Regole

- **Mai modificare codice** (R.Q2).
- **Mai decidere il verdict** (scope aggregator di code-review-protocol Fase 3).
- **task_package > 20 actions**: forza `severity-tiered` anche se config dice `all-in-one`.

## Limitazioni Cursor

- **Dispatch**: in Cursor il dev-agent va invocato manualmente dopo aver ricevuto il task_package dal router.
- **Weekly digest**: esegui lunedì mattina aggiornando i file digest manualmente.
